    <code code="10154-3" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Chief complaint Narrative - Reported"/>
    <title>Chief Complaint</title>
    <text><paragraph>More breathless, with more and greener sputum, for three days after a cold. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Paige called the clinic this morning, as his action plan says to when his symptoms worsen, and was seen the same day. A cold went around his church two weeks ago; five days ago he had a runny nose and sore throat, and for three days he has been more breathless than usual, now after half a block, with more sputum that has turned from clear to green and wheeze at night. He has used his albuterol four to five times a day, which helps for a few hours. He has taken his umeclidinium-vilanterol every morning. His home temperature was 37.8 °C last night. He has no chest pain, no blood in the sputum, no leg swelling and no new orthopnea. He is not smoking. He missed his two rehabilitation sessions this week. A home rapid test for COVID-19 and influenza was negative yesterday. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Onset</td><td>Three days ago, two days after a cold began</td></tr><tr><td>Severity</td><td>Breathless after half a block (worse than his usual one block); speaking in full sentences</td></tr><tr><td>Context</td><td>COPD on a LAMA with a LABA; no exacerbation in the past year</td></tr><tr><td>Associated signs and symptoms</td><td>More sputum, now green; wheeze at night; temperature to 37.8 °C; no chest pain, hemoptysis or leg swelling</td></tr><tr><td>Modifying factors</td><td>Albuterol helps for a few hours</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

