  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Moderate exacerbation of COPD (J44.1)</content>. A moderate exacerbation after a viral cold: more breathlessness and more, purulent sputum. The chest X-ray shows no pneumonia or pneumothorax, there is no sign of heart failure, and he is alert, not working hard to breathe and saturating 92 percent, so he can be treated at home. An antibiotic is indicated because the sputum is purulent and breathlessness has increased. A saturation of 92 percent by pulse oximetry may overstate his true oxygen level, but his arterial PaO2 was 70 mm Hg when stable, and he has no confusion or distress; he will check his saturation at home. [S]<list><item>Prednisone 40 mg each morning for five days.</item><item>Doxycycline 100 mg twice a day for five days, sitting up with a full glass of water.</item><item>Albuterol two to four inhalations with the spacer every four hours as needed.</item><item>Continue umeclidinium-vilanterol; technique checked and correct.</item><item>Call 911 or go to the emergency department for breathlessness at rest, confusion, chest pain, blue lips or a home saturation below 88 percent.</item><item>Nurse telephone call tomorrow and in three days.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">COPD, GOLD group B (J44.9)</content>. First exacerbation on maintenance therapy; the group and treatment will be reviewed once he has recovered. [S]<list><item>Resume pulmonary rehabilitation next week as tolerated.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: Global Strategy for the Prevention, Diagnosis and Management of COPD: 2025 Report (2025); Racial Bias in Pulse Oximetry Measurement (2020)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Review at the wellness visit in two weeks, or sooner as above. Next scheduled visit 2026-10-06: subsequent annual wellness visit. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
